 2 or the nuclear form is probably involved in transcriptional regulation via interaction with MLLT10"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12697670"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"15574124"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16336961"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17868029"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17878677"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18768470"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22052913"}],"value":"Interacts with INHBA and INHBB. Interacts with FN1. Interacts with ADAM12. Isoform 2 interacts with MLLT10; the interaction enhances MLLT10 in vitro transcriptional activity and self-association. Interacts with MSTN"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"INTERACTION","interactions":[{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O95633","intActId":"EBI-2625790"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O43184-2","geneName":"ADAM12","intActId":"EBI-2625865"},"numberOfExperiments":4,"organismDiffer":false}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","molecule":"Isoform 1","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"value":"Secreted","id":"SL-0243"}}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","molecule":"Isoform 2","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16150905"}],"value":"Although alternative initiation has been demonstrated and resulted in different localization, the major source of nuclear FSTL3 appears not to depend on translation initiation at Met-27 according to"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"value":"Nucleus","id":"SL-0191"}}]},{"commentType":"ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS","events":["Alternative initiation"],"isoforms":[{"name":{"value":"1"},"isoformIds":["O95633-1"],"isoformSequenceStatus":"Displayed"},{"name":{"value":"2"},"isoformIds":["O95633-2"],"sequenceIds":["VSP_038553"],"isoformSequenceStatus":"Described"}]},{"t